    words2 = lower(strsplit(lines2));

    % Find unique words in text1 that do not appear in text2
    uniqueWords = setdiff(words1, words2);
end
```

In this implementation, `textscan` reads each line as a separate input argument, rather than loading the entire file into memory. This makes it possible to work with very large files without running out of memory. Of course, this will slow down the computation slightly since it involves multiple I/O operations, but it's still much faster

