c_0 & c_1 & c_2\\
0 & c_0 & c_1\\
0 & 0 & c_0
\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix}
x_n\\ x_{n+1}\\ x_{n+2}
\end{bmatrix}

We can calculate the eigenvalues and eigenvectors of this matrix to determine if it is primitive or not (since a primitive LFSR generates all possible binary sequences). If it is not primitive, we can modify the coefficients until it becomes primitive.

Assuming that the given sequence is generated by a primitive LFSR, we can extract the coefficients from the characteristic polynomial of the matrix:

\det(XI - M) = X^3 - c_0X^2 - c_1X - c_2 = 0

Expanding the determinant and equating coefficients gives us:

c_0 = -1, c_1 = -c_2, where c_2 is any nonzero value.

Let's choose c_2 = 1. Then, c_1 = -c_2 = -1.

Now we have the coefficients, we can use the recurrence relation to calculate the values of x_8 and x_9:

x_8 = c_0x_5 + c_1x_6 + c_2x_7 = -x_5 - x_6 + x_7
x_9 = c_0x_6 + c_1x_7 + c_2x_8 = x_6 - x_7 - x_8

