1. Push Notifications (PN): This feature allows for real-time communication with users and can significantly increase user engagement and retention. To utilize PN, you can send targeted and personalized notifications based on user behavior, preferences, and location. Here's an example implementation using Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM):

```javascript
import firebase from 'firebase/app';
import 'firebase/messaging';

// Initialize Firebase project
firebase.initializeApp({
  apiKey: '<API_KEY>',
  authDomain: '<PROJECT_ID>.firebaseapp.com',
  databaseURL: 'https://<DATABASE_NAME>.firebaseio.com',
  projectId: '<PROJECT_ID>',
  storageBucket: '<BUCKET>.appspot.com',
  messagingSenderId: '<SENDER_ID>',
  appId: '<APP_ID>',
});

// Request permission for sending notifications
firebase.messaging().requestPermission()
  .then(() => {
    // Register device token for receiving PNs
    const token = firebase.messaging().getToken();
    console.log('Device Token: ', token);

    // Send targeted notification based on user behavior or preference
    const payload = {
      notification: {
        title: 'New Workout Plan Available! ',
        body: 'Check out our latest workout plan designed just for you.',
        click_action: '/workouts',
        icon: './assets/icons/workout.png',
      },
      to: token,
    };

    // Send notification using FCM API
    fetch('https://fcm.googleapis.com/fcm/send', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: {
        'Content-Type': 'application/json',
        Authorization: `Bearer ${firebase.auth().currentUser.accessToken}`,
      },
      body: JSON.stringify(payload),
    })
      .catch((error) => {
        console.error('Error sending notification: ', error);
      });
  })
  .catch((err) => {
    console.error('Unable to get permission to notify.', err);
  });
```

