4. Update `max_sum` with the maximum between the current `current_sum` and the current `current_sum` plus the elements from the current position to the end of the subarray (excluding the last element). This helps us find the maximum sum subarray starting from the current index.
5. Update `best_start` with the current index if the current `current_sum` is greater than the current `max_sum` minus the element at `best_start` index. This ensures we keep track of the starting index of the best subarray found so far.
6. Return `max_sum`.

